"""The website chat's answers to the questions patients ask the front desk most (from the receptionists' list,
SJDM branch): fillings, extractions, braces, TMJ, dentures, inlays/onlays, bridges, implants, wisdom teeth, root
canals and whitening.

These are checked before the chat's general routing, so a specific question ("pwede po bang magpabunot kahit
namamaga?") gets its own answer instead of a general one. Each entry:
- need: alternatives; each alternative is a list of words that must all be in the question (any order). Words
  of 3 letters or less must be whole words; longer ones may be part of a word ("pasta" matches "magpa-pasta").
  The best match is the alternative with the most and longest words.
- en / tl: the answer. General dental information only; the dentist confirms what applies to the patient.
- proc: the treatment it is about (the chat then offers its price and details).
- aspect: answer with that part of the treatment's own details instead (e.g. "recovery"), and no text of its own.
- act: "avail" = also show the next free online appointment times; "book" = offer booking first.
- price: the entry may answer a question that asks "how much" (others leave price questions to the price list).
- pending: the answer depends on a clinic policy that hasn't been confirmed yet, so it sends the patient to the
  branch. Replace the text once the clinic confirms (see POLICY_QUESTIONS).
"""

